MULTI-PROCESS: measuring the 2-device point only. A sub-mesh would
exclude whole processes, which then hold no shard of the array `sqd` gathers -- measured,
that raises FullyReplicatedShard inside process_allgather on exactly the excluded ranks.
For the curve, run this once per rank count and compare rows:
  for n in 1 2 4; do mpirun -n $n uv run --extra mpi python <this script> --devices mpi; done

==============================================================================
Claim 1+2: per-device memory and wall clock against device count
==============================================================================
Each row adds devices at FIXED N. A replicated term stays flat as devices double; a
sharded one halves. Speedup is against the 1-device arm, both warm. The energy is
asserted, not printed for inspection: a broken arm does less work and posts a better time.

 devices  baseline MB   solve MB  delta MB        ms       |dE|  speedup

