 devices  baseline MB   solve MB  delta MB        ms       |dE|  speedup
       2          0.0        0.0       0.0     961.8    0.0e+00  baseline

==============================================================================
VERDICT
==============================================================================
  energy invariant across (2,) devices: max |dE| within assertion bound.
  READ THE MEMORY COLUMN AS A CURVE, not as two points: `states` is replicated today
  (13*N per device, the term the (0,0) floor cannot shed) while the solver's O(N)
  vectors shard, so the honest expectation is a falling-but-not-halving delta.
  A FLAT delta means nothing sharded -- check the spec, not just the energy.

  Multi-NODE topology: these collectives crossed a network, not NVLink. A ratio
